WEBVTT

00:13.013 --> 00:15.640
LUCKY JERK

00:21.771 --> 00:22.605
Huh?!

00:28.445 --> 00:29.279
Oh my!

00:32.240 --> 00:33.241
How cute!

00:33.867 --> 00:35.994
What's wrong? Are you all alone?

00:39.080 --> 00:39.914
Huh?

00:48.256 --> 00:50.133
Please help me.

00:54.179 --> 00:55.221
A MONSTER APPEARS IN THE FOREST?

00:55.305 --> 00:56.639
This is today's newspaper!

00:57.223 --> 00:58.308
Look at this article.

00:59.267 --> 01:02.896
Could this be the "animal that
gives life" that En kept as a pet?

01:03.730 --> 01:05.065
What was it called...

01:05.148 --> 01:06.441
Chawantake?

01:06.524 --> 01:07.525
It's Kikurage.

01:08.026 --> 01:09.360
Good work! You may go now!

01:09.861 --> 01:10.987
Yes sir!

01:12.072 --> 01:14.491
It's easier to get information with more
people.

01:15.325 --> 01:17.660
Our organization is getting bigger and
bigger.

01:18.787 --> 01:19.621
Even now,

01:19.704 --> 01:23.208
workers are running at full capacity
tattooing new cross marks.

01:24.417 --> 01:26.753
What are you trying to do back there,
Natsuki?

01:28.004 --> 01:29.839
I thought maybe some smoke would
come out.

01:29.923 --> 01:30.757
All right, Ton.

01:31.341 --> 01:33.676
Go to that forest and investigate
this for us.

01:33.760 --> 01:34.803
Roger!

01:35.720 --> 01:39.641
Kikurage might get scared and run away if
Ton goes there alone.

01:40.433 --> 01:41.643
Natsuki, you go too.

01:42.143 --> 01:43.394
Huh? You want me?

01:43.895 --> 01:47.023
I'm sure the boss would want to obtain
Kikurage's Magic.

01:47.732 --> 01:49.609
Keep an eye out for this "monster."

01:49.692 --> 01:50.985
I'm counting on you.

01:51.653 --> 01:52.487
Right!

03:20.992 --> 03:22.911
THE BEGINNING

03:22.994 --> 03:24.454
PAYMENT

03:25.163 --> 03:26.748
Alright, this is the forest.

03:26.831 --> 03:29.959
The newspaper report said they were
somewhere near the stream.

03:35.048 --> 03:36.132
What's wrong, Natsuki?

03:36.216 --> 03:37.258
Oh, uh...

03:37.800 --> 03:38.635
It's just-

03:38.718 --> 03:41.971
about that smoke test that you did
for me the other day...

03:42.055 --> 03:42.889
Oh.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.267
For some reason, you got some pretty good
numbers.

03:47.060 --> 03:47.936
If you're curious,

03:48.019 --> 03:50.605
I'll test you in more detail back at
the mansion.

03:51.481 --> 03:52.732
That would be great!

03:52.815 --> 03:55.526
I want to be as useful as possible
to the boss!

03:56.027 --> 03:58.696
I'll get stronger! Just like you and the
others, Ton.

03:58.780 --> 04:01.783
Well, for now, it doesn't seem
like there's much you can do.

04:01.866 --> 04:02.825
Hey!

04:08.748 --> 04:09.582
Jeez...

04:09.666 --> 04:12.252
she loves crawling through these tight
spaces, huh?

04:13.544 --> 04:15.338
Was there someone just here?

04:16.297 --> 04:17.548
I've got a blister...

04:18.591 --> 04:21.427
I wish Kikurage had bigger legs. This is
taking forever.

04:23.471 --> 04:25.014
It's already been four days.

04:25.515 --> 04:27.600
My heel is bleeding...!

04:28.559 --> 04:30.853
- Remember! This is all about reviving
- My blister burst too!

04:30.937 --> 04:31.980
The En Family!

04:34.524 --> 04:36.526
FIVE DAYS AGO

04:40.196 --> 04:42.240
It can't be... The En Mansion...

04:42.740 --> 04:45.994
I can't believe they took our
mansion away from us...

04:46.703 --> 04:49.038
Are these the only ones who survived?

04:49.706 --> 04:51.791
What a bunch of half-dead losers.

04:53.835 --> 04:56.546
Thank you. Because of you and your magic,

04:56.629 --> 04:58.506
we were able to escape the mansion.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.967
If you hadn't shown up

05:01.467 --> 05:04.262
everybody here would certainly be
dead right now.

05:05.346 --> 05:07.974
Even so... I could've saved more people...

05:08.558 --> 05:09.392
I could have...

05:11.269 --> 05:13.771
Don't worry, you did more than enough.

05:14.564 --> 05:16.190
Mr. Turkey, who is this?

05:16.899 --> 05:19.027
You! Have you forgotten me too?

05:20.111 --> 05:20.945
I, ah...

05:21.571 --> 05:23.823
Fujita, you're being extremely rude.

05:23.906 --> 05:26.492
He's been a member since the family was
formed.

05:26.576 --> 05:27.910
His name is...

05:29.370 --> 05:30.538
His name is...

05:31.039 --> 05:32.206
Ah... em...

05:33.833 --> 05:34.917
Never mind.

05:38.129 --> 05:39.088
Before the attack,

05:39.589 --> 05:41.924
I was also able to rescue Shin and Noi.

05:42.008 --> 05:43.926
The Cross-Eyes nearly killed them.

05:44.010 --> 05:47.889
That was how I managed to take something
from the enemy without them knowing.

05:48.848 --> 05:50.683
Mr. En's severed head.

05:51.768 --> 05:52.769
How wonderful!

05:52.852 --> 05:54.437
You got it back!

05:55.021 --> 05:57.648
But, the devil tumor inside his head

05:58.149 --> 05:59.901
had already been removed.

06:01.027 --> 06:02.028
N-No way...

06:02.612 --> 06:04.322
That means En is already...

06:04.822 --> 06:07.033
No, there's still some hope for him.

06:07.533 --> 06:10.536
If we get Mr. En's devil tumor back from
the Cross-Eyes,

06:10.620 --> 06:13.247
ask Noi to repair his body,

06:13.331 --> 06:15.291
and use Kikurage's Magic...

06:15.375 --> 06:16.376
Of course!

06:17.585 --> 06:20.463
It's too bad that Kikurage is still
missing...

06:20.546 --> 06:21.672
- I see.
- Huh?

06:22.173 --> 06:25.134
That's where my particular skills come
in again.

06:25.676 --> 06:27.720
Exactly. Fujita,

06:27.804 --> 06:28.971
we must find Kikurage.

06:29.055 --> 06:30.890
Can I entrust the search to you?

06:32.600 --> 06:34.394
I swear... I'll do it!

06:34.477 --> 06:37.146
Whatever it takes to revive Mister En!

06:39.273 --> 06:40.358
And so here we are...

06:40.900 --> 06:44.278
following the Kikurage doll that
Mr. Turkey made...

06:44.779 --> 06:47.031
but did he have to make her walk so slow?

06:47.115 --> 06:48.116
It's so bad.

06:49.617 --> 06:52.495
Ebisu!
Why the hell are you on this mission?

06:52.995 --> 06:54.080
I brought snacks...

06:54.163 --> 06:55.164
for-

06:55.248 --> 06:56.082
for Kikurage...

06:57.041 --> 06:57.875
That's right.

06:58.376 --> 07:01.087
You were always closer to Kikurage
than I was.

07:01.754 --> 07:02.588
All right.

07:02.672 --> 07:05.425
Once we find Kikurage, I'll leave her
to you.

07:07.510 --> 07:11.013
I- I can't! My body is at it's limit!

07:16.436 --> 07:18.813
Is that...? It's Kikurage's voice!

07:18.896 --> 07:20.022
I'm sure of it!

07:20.106 --> 07:22.191
I'm gonna call this in to Sho!

07:22.733 --> 07:26.070
- Kikurage, please be okay.
- Little butt, little butt, little butt.

07:28.364 --> 07:29.490
Kikurage...

07:30.241 --> 07:33.828
You don't need to stay here with me
anymore.

07:34.495 --> 07:36.831
I'm gonna die soon.

07:39.542 --> 07:40.376
Sorry, En.

07:40.460 --> 07:42.587
You entrusted Kikurage to me and
me alone,

07:44.380 --> 07:48.426
but in the end, I couldn't protect her
like you expected!

07:49.594 --> 07:51.512
I found her! That's Kikurage!

07:51.596 --> 07:53.055
Oh, there she is!

07:53.139 --> 07:54.390
Th-The Cross-Eyes?

07:54.474 --> 07:56.267
Run, Kikurage! Run!

07:58.519 --> 08:00.438
Heh! Don't even try to run.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.400
I reeled her in!

08:04.484 --> 08:05.610
You scumbags!

08:05.693 --> 08:06.903
Let go of Kikurage!

08:07.403 --> 08:09.197
How dare you kill my En!

08:09.280 --> 08:10.406
I'll kill you all!

08:10.907 --> 08:12.575
Hey, you're Chota, aren't you?

08:13.409 --> 08:16.162
Your name was on the list of En
Family officers.

08:16.704 --> 08:19.373
Guess I'll take your head while
I'm at it.

08:19.957 --> 08:21.209
You bastard!

08:21.292 --> 08:22.251
It's okay.

08:22.752 --> 08:25.505
I'll kill you in one shot so you
barley feel a thing.

08:25.588 --> 08:26.422
- Ton!
- Huh?

08:26.506 --> 08:27.340
This is bad!

08:27.965 --> 08:29.550
There's another Kikurage...

08:30.092 --> 08:30.927
What?!

08:34.055 --> 08:36.766
I didn't expect we'd run into
the Cross-Eyes out here.

08:38.434 --> 08:40.645
If we don't move, they'll kill
both of them.

08:41.145 --> 08:45.066
At the same time, I'm not at all
confident we can beat them.

08:51.864 --> 08:52.865
E-Ebisu?

08:59.288 --> 09:00.122
What's that?!

09:07.505 --> 09:09.090
A- A monster?

09:09.173 --> 09:10.174
Natsuki!

09:17.890 --> 09:19.767
We got another En Family member!

09:23.729 --> 09:25.022
Mr. Chota, are you okay?

09:25.523 --> 09:26.816
Oh, Fujita!

09:27.400 --> 09:29.277
Ebisu just... What on earth is that?

09:29.777 --> 09:33.197
I'm sure that the devil's hairpin is
still inside her head, plus the

09:33.281 --> 09:35.950
emotional agitation of seeing Kikurage in
danger

09:36.033 --> 09:38.995
must have affected her Magic somehow to
create this!

09:51.841 --> 09:52.758
Now what is that?

10:04.228 --> 10:05.813
Ebisu's attacks have no effect!

10:05.896 --> 10:06.814
My goodness.

10:06.897 --> 10:08.232
That's defense-type Magic.

10:08.899 --> 10:11.611
I didn't know there was a Cross-Eyes
who could use it.

10:13.904 --> 10:15.489
This is bad! We're out of time!

10:15.573 --> 10:16.532
Ebisu! Oh!

10:17.033 --> 10:17.908
Fujita!

10:18.409 --> 10:20.161
Is everyone okay?

10:24.540 --> 10:27.376
So this Kikurage was a fake?

10:27.877 --> 10:30.046
But Natsuki is the real surprise.

10:31.380 --> 10:34.842
To think that cut would accidentally
open her smoke veins...

10:35.760 --> 10:37.136
Anyway Natsuki, I gotta say

10:37.637 --> 10:39.639
you're useful to the boss now alright.

10:40.139 --> 10:40.973
Very useful.

10:44.477 --> 10:46.937
ADVANCED MAGIC

10:49.982 --> 10:51.400
FLOOD OF CUSTOMERS

10:51.484 --> 10:53.944
RECEPTION

10:56.113 --> 10:57.073
Where am I?

10:57.573 --> 10:58.908
What is this place?

11:29.647 --> 11:30.481
Hm?

11:37.655 --> 11:38.656
Who are you?

11:41.701 --> 11:43.577
Where am I? What is this place?

11:44.245 --> 11:46.122
You're holding out on me, aren't you?

11:49.458 --> 11:51.168
Will you drop that already!?

11:51.252 --> 11:53.921
I told you, there's nothing I can do
about it.

11:54.630 --> 11:56.966
I'm not fighting back, end of story!

12:12.314 --> 12:13.149
Y-You're...!

12:16.444 --> 12:17.278
Aikawa.

12:18.571 --> 12:19.447
Aikawa.

12:22.491 --> 12:23.325
Are you okay?

12:23.826 --> 12:25.953
You were talking a lot in your sleep.

12:26.036 --> 12:26.871
Yeah...

12:27.913 --> 12:30.708
So I guess you have nightmares too, huh?

12:37.339 --> 12:40.176
How are you, Risu?
How's your body feeling now?

12:40.676 --> 12:42.720
I'm feeling much better now, thanks.

12:43.304 --> 12:47.308
Sorry again, you know you didn't have to
take care of me for two whole days.

12:47.391 --> 12:49.810
Don't worry about it. Well, I'm off.

12:49.894 --> 12:50.936
Be back soon.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.272
- Aikawa.
- Hm?

12:53.773 --> 12:57.443
You're the only person I know who
cares about me enough to stay here.

12:58.444 --> 12:59.278
Thank you.

13:00.529 --> 13:01.906
Well yeah, what'd you expect?

13:01.989 --> 13:03.449
I'm your partner after all.

13:03.532 --> 13:04.575
See ya!

13:04.658 --> 13:06.452
You better get plenty of rest.

13:09.205 --> 13:12.166
TACHIKAWA APARTMENTS

13:14.293 --> 13:16.754
What was that place in my dream just now...

13:17.379 --> 13:20.216
and who was that man lighting a
cigarette?

13:23.385 --> 13:26.639
Let's forget it...
I don't want to think about anything...

13:28.474 --> 13:29.350
All I want...

13:29.850 --> 13:33.687
is to live a normal life as a Sorcerer,
same as anyone else.

13:34.355 --> 13:35.689
But that has me thinking...

13:37.608 --> 13:41.320
Maybe... I shouldn't see Risu anymore.

13:43.239 --> 13:44.698
Another headache...

13:45.199 --> 13:46.408
Damn it.

13:47.076 --> 13:49.078
Damn it... Damn it!

13:58.420 --> 14:00.381
Put some oil on me, Hayes.

14:00.965 --> 14:01.799
Okay.

14:02.675 --> 14:05.302
Haru, is there any point in doing this?

14:05.386 --> 14:06.512
You're a devil.

14:06.595 --> 14:08.556
It's to set the mood, baby.

14:13.811 --> 14:14.645
Good job.

14:16.564 --> 14:17.398
Hmm...

14:18.232 --> 14:19.066
Y'know Hayes,

14:19.149 --> 14:21.151
I've been thinking this for a while,

14:21.235 --> 14:23.445
but I'm not really into this look of
yours.

14:23.946 --> 14:24.905
Huh?

14:24.989 --> 14:26.991
We kinda look like mother and son.

14:27.074 --> 14:29.076
Ultimate Devil power!

14:32.997 --> 14:35.791
Huh?! Whoa! You turned me into an adult!

14:35.875 --> 14:36.750
Just like that!

14:37.543 --> 14:39.670
You even conjured my glasses from
nothing!

14:40.212 --> 14:43.924
It feels like every day I spend with you
shatters the part of my mind that

14:44.008 --> 14:46.010
believes in science further and further.

14:47.261 --> 14:48.846
Well Hayes, how about it?

14:51.056 --> 14:53.475
Why don't you come live with me in Hell?

14:54.184 --> 14:56.896
It'll beat living in that garbage
dump Hole.

14:59.106 --> 15:01.609
Choosing between Hell or the Hole, huh?

15:02.276 --> 15:03.402
That's a tough choice.

15:05.112 --> 15:07.656
- You belong to me, human!
- You belong to me, human!

15:07.740 --> 15:09.575
- You will do as I say! Understand?
- You will do as I say! Understand?

15:09.658 --> 15:11.327
You know, these sudden changes in

15:11.410 --> 15:13.579
- your appearance are really jarring!
- I was about to die...

15:13.662 --> 15:15.414
- I was about to die...
- Anyway,

15:15.915 --> 15:19.793
it's been on my mind for a while,
but I want to try and find Ai.

15:20.294 --> 15:22.713
- Is it really that important to
- Is it really that important to

15:22.796 --> 15:24.048
- you, honey?
- you, honey?

15:24.131 --> 15:25.215
Of course it's important.

15:25.299 --> 15:28.886
If I can prove that it's possible
to be able to turn a human being into a

15:28.969 --> 15:30.554
sorcerer through the power of science-

15:30.638 --> 15:33.015
that will have huge implications on my
research!

15:33.098 --> 15:34.016
I get it, I get it...

15:34.099 --> 15:34.975
I get it, I get it...

15:35.059 --> 15:37.144
- I'll help you find him.
- I'll help you find him.

15:37.227 --> 15:38.062
Thank you, Haru!

15:38.145 --> 15:40.314
But first, uh... can you change my body
back?

15:41.815 --> 15:43.525
This feels really weird.

15:43.609 --> 15:45.194
- Why?
- Why?

15:49.365 --> 15:50.324
Package for you.

15:50.407 --> 15:51.492
Thank you.

15:52.493 --> 15:54.203
Thank goodness it arrived safe.

15:54.828 --> 15:55.746
Now then...

16:06.632 --> 16:07.883
I can't believe it.

16:08.384 --> 16:12.012
She's wearing a suit twice as heavy as
the one used in the regular devil

16:12.096 --> 16:14.556
exam, and it's not giving her any trouble
at all!

16:19.186 --> 16:20.688
Next is the rinse!

16:20.771 --> 16:21.647
Nikaido!

16:22.147 --> 16:23.023
Huh?

16:23.107 --> 16:24.358
Come down, let's eat!

16:28.779 --> 16:29.613
Tada,

16:29.697 --> 16:32.783
another hearty meal of the finest
devil meat cuisine!

16:33.617 --> 16:35.619
We're having Devil meat again?

16:35.703 --> 16:37.496
This is all part of your training.

16:38.706 --> 16:41.000
Wait... this isn't what I think
it is, right?

16:41.709 --> 16:42.918
Sure it looks gross,

16:43.002 --> 16:44.753
but it tastes fantastic.

16:46.130 --> 16:46.964
Asu...

16:47.506 --> 16:49.216
What are we really doing here?

16:49.299 --> 16:51.719
It feels like I'm training for the Devil
exam,

16:52.261 --> 16:55.014
but I'm definitely not planning
to become a devil.

16:55.514 --> 16:56.640
Right,

16:56.724 --> 16:58.225
when you were younger,

16:58.308 --> 17:00.060
you couldn't control your magic.

17:00.561 --> 17:04.064
And I think a big part of why is
because you weren't able to produce

17:04.148 --> 17:05.107
enough smoke.

17:05.190 --> 17:07.151
By training for the devil exam,

17:07.234 --> 17:09.153
that's exactly what you're practicing.

17:11.905 --> 17:12.740
Okay,

17:12.823 --> 17:15.826
try to produce as much smoke as you can.

17:15.909 --> 17:16.952
Right.

17:25.836 --> 17:26.879
Don't be afraid.

17:27.713 --> 17:30.466
You've trained to produce all the smoke
you'll need.

17:30.549 --> 17:33.218
I'm sure that's why you failed when you
were young.

17:33.802 --> 17:34.636
Asu...

17:52.654 --> 17:53.864
Don't look away from it!

17:53.947 --> 17:54.907
Keep making smoke!

17:54.990 --> 17:56.492
Make as much of it as you can!

18:03.749 --> 18:04.583
The cube!

18:05.667 --> 18:07.044
It changed...?!

18:08.170 --> 18:12.299
Nikaido, produce more smoke! I'm sure
it'll change even more!

18:14.093 --> 18:15.385
I... can't...

18:15.886 --> 18:17.596
It's too much!

18:21.850 --> 18:22.684
Nikaido!

18:25.604 --> 18:26.605
LIBRARY, CAFETERIA

18:26.688 --> 18:29.399
Aikawa! Get back here!

18:30.776 --> 18:31.610
Whoa!

18:33.862 --> 18:37.032
Hand over the ingredients for the
school lunch, you scumbag!

18:37.116 --> 18:39.743
Damn it... Looks like I'm cornered...

18:39.827 --> 18:43.539
If you come any closer, I may fall off
the edge and die!

18:44.039 --> 18:45.541
Sounds like a great idea!

18:45.624 --> 18:49.086
Go ahead and die! Smash your brains
against the ground!

18:49.169 --> 18:50.129
You're awful!

18:52.422 --> 18:54.925
- Aikawa?!
- Just kidding!

18:55.509 --> 18:56.343
Whoa!

18:57.928 --> 18:59.388
Smell ya later!

19:10.149 --> 19:14.111
He comes to school, eats, plays,
and sleeps.

19:14.611 --> 19:17.072
He's the same Aikawa as before...

19:18.323 --> 19:19.616
It's hard to accept...

19:20.325 --> 19:22.369
he would tell someone about my Magic.

19:22.452 --> 19:25.497
Especially not someone from the
Cross-Eyes.

19:26.915 --> 19:28.208
Hm? Hey there!

19:28.292 --> 19:29.251
Risu, is that you?!

19:29.334 --> 19:31.461
- Shhh!
- It's been a while!

19:31.545 --> 19:32.379
Risu?

19:36.133 --> 19:39.178
I didn't know you were here,
you should've said something!

19:43.140 --> 19:43.974
Aikawa...

19:44.600 --> 19:46.476
you're full of mysteries, aren't you?

19:47.019 --> 19:49.188
Hm? Full of mysteries?

19:49.271 --> 19:50.189
Like what?

19:50.689 --> 19:53.317
Like where you actually live...

19:53.817 --> 19:56.278
Or where you make money to eat...

19:56.361 --> 19:57.487
Basically, everything!

19:59.281 --> 20:02.993
You've still never told me what kind of
Magic-user you are!

20:03.493 --> 20:06.997
Even though I haven't hidden anything
from you!

20:07.080 --> 20:07.915
Risu!

20:07.998 --> 20:11.335
L-Like I told you, I can only produce a
little bit of smoke.

20:11.835 --> 20:14.421
- Don't play dumb with me!
- Don't play dumb with me!

20:14.504 --> 20:16.798
You're the only one I've ever told about
my Magic!

20:16.882 --> 20:19.760
But you just had to run and tell
someone my secret!

20:19.843 --> 20:20.928
That's why

20:21.011 --> 20:22.095
I was killed!

20:22.179 --> 20:23.597
It's not like that, Risu.

20:23.680 --> 20:24.848
Listen to me. I didn't-

20:24.932 --> 20:26.725
I can't believe a single damn word you
say!

20:26.808 --> 20:28.936
I can't believe a single damn word you
say!

20:29.019 --> 20:31.104
The Cross-Eyes will tell me the truth,

20:31.188 --> 20:33.273
even if I have to tear it out of them!

20:33.357 --> 20:34.983
My current power is more than enough for

20:35.067 --> 20:35.984
- that.
- Risu!

20:36.485 --> 20:37.486
Hey, wait!

20:38.987 --> 20:40.322
Does that mean he's going...

20:40.989 --> 20:42.324
to En's mansion?

20:48.747 --> 20:50.249
Sorry I pushed you so hard.

20:50.791 --> 20:52.626
It's okay. But I was surprised.

20:53.126 --> 20:55.504
I never thought the cube would transform.

20:56.255 --> 20:57.089
Alright,

20:57.172 --> 21:00.300
now what the hell do I have to
do to master all of this magic?

21:01.051 --> 21:01.885
Hmm...

21:04.388 --> 21:06.848
Wait, this reminds me of something I read
about.

21:06.932 --> 21:08.517
It's a similar case to yours.

21:10.102 --> 21:11.853
But it was a long time ago...

21:12.896 --> 21:15.941
If only I could find that book
and read it again somehow...

21:17.401 --> 21:18.777
Well, where is it now? Huh?

21:19.653 --> 21:21.238
It's written in devil language.

21:21.780 --> 21:24.866
The only Sorcerer who has it... would be
Mister En!

21:24.950 --> 21:26.285
Back to the mansion, then?

21:27.411 --> 21:28.745
Okay, let's go!

21:30.414 --> 21:33.250
At the moment, it's been occupied by the
Cross-Eyes

21:34.001 --> 21:35.043
It's very dangerous.

21:35.627 --> 21:39.214
Plus, there's a good chance that they've
already identified you as En's

21:39.298 --> 21:40.674
former Partner.

21:41.675 --> 21:44.344
So searching the place for a small
book will take time.

21:44.428 --> 21:46.763
That means, we'll need a pretty good
disguise.

21:47.389 --> 21:48.223
A disguise?

21:48.307 --> 21:49.266
Exaclty,

21:49.349 --> 21:50.767
that's where this comes in.

21:52.477 --> 21:56.106
Once you take off your clothes,
step inside this box, put the bottles in

21:56.189 --> 21:57.858
the machine, and pull the lever.

21:57.941 --> 21:58.900
Hmm...

22:00.027 --> 22:01.111
What a relief,

22:01.194 --> 22:03.196
I can finally take off this armor.

22:03.697 --> 22:04.823
Huh?

22:05.615 --> 22:08.618
A set of clothes for me to wear once I've
transformed?

22:08.702 --> 22:11.330
Finally, a chance to wear a
decent outfit.

22:13.040 --> 22:14.207
Let's see...

22:15.667 --> 22:18.295
Set the bottles here and here...

22:19.087 --> 22:20.255
Guess I pull the lever.

22:21.298 --> 22:22.507
OCCUPIED

24:20.709 --> 24:21.751
THE END

24:22.252 --> 24:24.087
What we learned in Episode twenty-two.

24:24.171 --> 24:25.922
Sho saved the En Family.

24:26.006 --> 24:27.924
Natsuki's magic repels everything.

24:28.008 --> 24:29.926
Nikaido's magic is immature.

24:30.010 --> 24:32.179
What we're going to learn in Episode
twenty-three.

24:32.262 --> 24:34.055
It's still... lost in chaos.

24:34.139 --> 24:36.558
This is Dorohedoro!
